# ============================================================================
# NO CATCH-ALL RULE HERE — this is intentional.
#
# A blanket `/*  /en/:splat  301` rule is UNSAFE: on Cloudflare Pages this file
# is evaluated by the asset server for ANY path that doesn't resolve to a built
# file. That includes locale-prefixed paths that 404 (e.g. /en/does-not-exist).
# For those, the splat would re-prepend /en/ on every hop:
#     /en/en → /en/en/en → /en/en/en/en → …  (infinite 301 loop)
# which is exactly what produced the long /en/en/en/… URLs.
#
# The generic "non-prefixed legacy path → /en" redirect is handled instead by
# functions/_middleware.ts (its `if (!pathLocale)` branch). That runs BEFORE the
# asset server, is locale-aware, and only prepends /en/ to paths that do NOT
# already start with a known locale — so it can never loop. Unmatched
# locale-prefixed paths now fall through to a normal 404, which is the correct
# SEO signal.
# ============================================================================
